  "result": "Perfect! All 254 tests pass. The customer statements feature is complete:\n\n**Created src/statements.js:**\n- `statement(customerId, invoices, asOf)` function that generates customer statements\n  - Validates customer exists (CUSTOMER_NOT_FOUND)\n  - Validates asOf date format (DATE_INVALID)\n  - Filters invoices for:\n    - Specified customer (ID normalized with trim + uppercase)\n    - Status 'issued', 'partially_paid', or 'paid'\n    - issueDate on or before asOf\n  - Returns statement object with:\n    - Normalized customerId\n    - invoices array with { number, issueDate, dueDate, total, due }\n    - dueDate field included when present on invoice\n    - due calculated using balanceDue from payments module\n    - Sorted by issueDate (ascending)\n    - totalDue = sum of all due amounts\n  - No mutation of input data\n\n**Created test/statements.test.js with 24 tests covering:**\n- Single invoice statement\n- Multiple invoices for same customer\n- Filtering by customer (excludes other customers)\n- Date filtering (before/on/after asOf)\n- Sorting by issueDate ascending\n- totalDue calculation\n- Draft invoice filtering (excluded)\n- Paid invoices (due = 0)\n- Partially paid invoices (remaining due)\n- Multiple customers\n- Unknown customer handling\n- Invalid date handling\n- ID normalization (case, whitespace)\n- Empty customer statements\n- Long date ranges\n- Invoices with dueDate, vouchers, and discounts\n- Immutability verification",
